  "reason": "The best result so far is config_033 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted, multimodal, multiprofile) at 0.713 accuracy. The image-only experiments show both encoders are weak in isolation (resnet50: 0.208, ViT-L: 0.227), but in a multimodal setting a richer image representation could provide more complementary signal. Config_039 is a clean single-variable change from config_033—swapping resnet50 for imagenet_vit_l—while keeping the proven-best RNA encoder (scvi_n200), aggregation (transformer), fusion (weighted), and profile setting (multiprofile). ViT-L's global self-attention may capture spatial patterns in cellular images that ResNet's local receptive fields miss, potentially improving the multimodal fusion. This is the highest-leverage single change to test: if it improves on 0.713, we find a new best; if not, we confirm resnet50 is sufficient and the remaining experiment can explore fusion method (concat vs weighted) or other refinements."
